    {
      "id": "0c47ab942dd5dbde2d869397dcb7bb2829e98854",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 681221230,
          "type": null,
          "body": "1. Debian 11, cmake-3.18.4, gcc-10.2.1, gnutls-3.7.1\n2. cmd\n3. Makefile\n4.\n```\n[ 85%] Building C object epan/CMakeFiles/epan.dir/secrets.c.o\n/home/toni/git/wireshark/epan/secrets.c:63:8: error: unknown type name ‘uat_t’\n  63 | static uat_t *pkcs11_libs_uat;\n     |        ^~~~~\n```\n\nThe issue here is that `HAVE_GNUTLS_PKCS11` always defined if GnuTLS was found and has a decent version (and the pkcs11 symbol/header exists).\n\nSo I see two ways of fixing that issue. One way you are seeing right now and the other one would be replacing the line in [CMakeLists.txt:1297](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/CMakeLists.txt#L1297) with: `if(ENABLE_GNUTLS AND GNUTLS_FOUND AND NOT GNUTLS_VERSION VERSION_LESS \"3.4.0\")`",
          "author": {
            "id": 1898071,
            "username": "utoni",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Toni",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9607299dd8cde6fbc1e0b387e06a6d71a81d14e3e6fc5e4210c72f8318f9581d?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/utoni"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-18T12:33:20.494Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-18T12:34:25.938Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117327572,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4223,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a29f3c2e6f71d4ccd8a90906db89b15e374d5d81",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 681303416,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> The issue here is that `HAVE_GNUTLS_PKCS11` always defined if GnuTLS was found\n\nGiven that 1) epan/secrets.c includes <epan/uat.h> iff `HAVE_LIBGNUTLS` is defined, *irregardless of whether `HAVE_GNUTLS_PKCS11` is defined*, 2) <epan/uat.h> defines `uat_t` (as an opaque structure, so that you can declare a `uat_t *` even though you can't declare a `uat_t`), and 3) the problem in question is that `uat_t` isn't defined at all, it appears that `HAVE_LIBGNUTLS` is not defined.\n\nI.e., GnuTLS was *not* found, so the issue cannot be that \"`HAVE_GNUTLS_PKCS11` always defined if GnuTLS was found and has a decent version\" - it must be that, somehow, `HAVE_GNUTLS_PKCS11`, is getting defined even if GnuTLS *wasn't* found (because, in this case, *we shouldn't even have been trying to find it*, given that  `ENABLE_GNUTLS` is false).\n\nCMakeLists.txt does:\n\n```       \n# Support for TLS decryption using RSA private keys.\nws_find_package(GNUTLS ENABLE_GNUTLS HAVE_LIBGNUTLS \"3.3.0\")\n```\n\nand `ws_find_package()` is defined as\n\n```\n# ws_find_package(<PackageName>\n#             <CMakeOptions.txt boolean variable>\n#             <cmakeconfig.h.in macro definition>\n#             [remaining find_package() arguments])\nmacro(ws_find_package _package_name _enable_package _package_cmakedefine)\n\tif(${_enable_package})\n\t\t# Clear outdated cache variables if not already.\n\t\treset_find_package(${_package_name})\n\t\tfind_package(${_package_name} ${ARGN})\n\t\tif(${_package_name}_FOUND)\n\t\t\tset(${_package_cmakedefine} 1)\n\t\tendif()\n\tendif()\nendmacro()\n```\n\nso `find_package()` should not be called on the package `GNUTLS` if `ENABLE_GNUTLS` is false.\n\n`HAVE_GNUTLS_PKCS11` is defined by\n\n```\nif(GNUTLS_FOUND AND NOT GNUTLS_VERSION VERSION_LESS \"3.4.0\")\n\t# Calculating public keys from PKCS #11 private keys requires GnuTLS\n\t# 3.4.0 or greater.\n\t#\n\t# Check that the support is present in case GnuTLS was compiled\n\t# --without-p11-kit as macos-setup.sh did until December 2020.\n\tcmake_push_check_state()\n\tif(WIN32)\n\t\tset(CMAKE_REQUIRED_DEFINITIONS -Dssize_t=int)\n\tendif()\n\tset(CMAKE_REQUIRED_INCLUDES ${GNUTLS_INCLUDE_DIRS})\n\tset(CMAKE_REQUIRED_LIBRARIES ${GNUTLS_LIBRARIES})\n\tcheck_symbol_exists(gnutls_pkcs11_obj_list_import_url4 gnutls/pkcs11.h HAVE_GNUTLS_PKCS11)\n\tcmake_pop_check_state()\nendif()\n```\n\nand so should only be defined if `GNUTLS_FOUND` is defined.\n\nWhat do the commands\n\n    egrep GNUTLS config.h\n\nand\n\n    egrep GNUTLS CMakeCache.txt\n\nprint when run in your build directory?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-18T20:10:20.913Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-18T20:10:20.913Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117327572,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4223,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
